    "visibleText": "Schedule – PyCon Hong Kong 2021 - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Schedule – PyCon Hong Kong 2021 Posted on September 12, 2021 July 20, 2025 October 8, 2021 (Friday) Time (UTC+8) English Tracks 10:30-10:40 Opening 10:40-11:10 MySQL Operator for Kubernetes Mr. Ryan Kuan / MySQL 11:25-11:55 Intelligent pricing for an e-commerce platform Mr. Alex Zhang, Mr. Ben Wong / PCCW-HKT 12:00-14:00 Lunch 14:00-14:30 Applying ML Models to Cooling Load Prediction for Higher Energy Efficiency in Buildings – A Case Study Mr. Benny Tam / Hong Kong / ATAL Building Services Engineering Ltd 14:45-15:15 How Azure Machine Learning and Cognitive Services can Make Your Life Easier Mr. Kinfey Lo / Hong Kong / Microsoft 15:15-15:45 Break 15:45-16:15 Neural Prophet – A powerful AI framework for Time Series Models Mr. Kalyan Prasad / India 16:30-17:00 Bridging the Data Science Gap in Production ML with Tempo Mr. Alejandro Saucedo / London / The Institute for Ethical AI & Machine Learning October 9, 2021 (Saturday) Time (UTC+8) English Track Cantonese Track Education Track 10:30-11:00 Is the news media polarized? Or are we conditioned to think it is? Ms. Aroma Rodrigues / USA / UMass Amherst 廣東話自肥企画 Cantonese Selfish Project Mr. Scotty Kwok / Hong Kong / Sebit Company Limited 11:15-11:45 Financial Data Forecaster Ms. Anshika Rajiv / Hong Kong / Computer Science Student at the University of Hong Kong Building simple Transformer model for custom data Ms. Winnie Yeung / Hong Kong / Visa 12:00-14:00 Lunch 14:00-14:30 Metaclasses : The Realm of Metaprogramming Ms. Pratibha Jagnere / Malaysia Introduction to Koalas Mr. Wong Ho Wa / Hong Kong Guide your children into the realm of AI with coding Mr. Adam Nip / AI Lab 14:45-15:15 Securing Django Applications Mr. Gajendra Deshpande / India / KLS Gogte Institute of Technology, India Using PySide2 and Qt Quick as GUI for IoT Project on Raspberry Pi Mr. Arnold Chan / Hong Kong Using AWS AI and Amazon Sumerian in IT Education Mr. Cyrus Wong / IVE 15:15-15:45 Break 15:45-16:15 Python Versions and Dependencies Made Easy Mr. Sebastian Witowski / Poland MySQL Shell is your python friend #2 Mr. Ivan Ma / Hong Kong / MySQL Student journey in Python – Part 1 Ms. Vivian Fung (Moderator) 16:30-17:00 Unmasking the neglected crowd in the genome Ms. Claire Chung / Hong Kong / The Chinese University of Hong Kong; OSHK; HKOSCON EXCO Student journey in Python – Part 2 Ms. Vivian Fung (Moderator) 17:15-17:45 From Zero to Hero, My Python journey to the West Ms. Cheuk Ting Ho / London, UK / TerminusDB 17:50-17:55 Closing Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2026 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2020 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Intelligent pricing for an e-commerce platform ← Privacy Policy Statement 2021"
