    "visibleText": "Introduction to Koalas - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Introduction to Koalas Posted on September 1, 2021 February 16, 2022 Pandas is a well-known library for data scientist yet it does not scale. Koalas provides a pandas interface for big data manipulation in spark environment. In this session, koalas usage will be demonstrated for distributed data frame manipulation. Speaker: Mr. Wong Ho Wa / Hong Kong - GitHub , Twitter , LinkedIn Language: Cantonese Date and Time : October 9, 2021 / 14:00-14:30 (UTC+8) Speaker Introduction Wong Ho Wa is currently a data scientist in a luxury fashion industry and conveyor of open data working group, Internet Society Hong Kong. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2026 2025 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2020 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Building simple Transformer model for custom data ← Neural Prophet – A powerful AI framework for Time Series Models"
